Kertzer begins his fascinating investigation of the dramatic kidnapping, and shows how the deep-rooted antisemitism of the Catholic Church would eventually contribute to the collapse of its temporal power in Italy. As Edgardo's parents desperately search for a way to get their son back, they learn why he - out of all their eight children - was taken. Years earlier, the family's Catholic serving girl, fearful that the infant might die of an illness, had secretly baptized him (or so she claimed). Edgardo recovered, but when the story reached the Bologna inquisitor, the result was his order for Edgardo to be seized and sent to a special monastery where Jews were converted into good Catholics. His justification in Church teachings: No Christian child could be raised by Jewish parents. The case of Edgardo Mortara became an international cause celebre.","publicationYear":1997,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Conversion to Christianity","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Jews","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Christian converts from Judaism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Jews, italy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-kidnapping-of-edgardo-mortara-david-i-kertzer"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_